A Unix operating system ships conﬁgured to run this command every night:


          find /tmp -atime +3 -exec safeunlink {} ;


 The eﬀect is to ﬁnd every ﬁle that has not been accessed in more than three days
  under the directory /tmp and run the safeunlink command on that ﬁle’s pathname.
  safeunlink deletes a ﬁle. Its implementation is below.

 Assume path to components takes a Unix pathname separated by “/” characters and
    splits it into an NULL-terminated array of strings, one for each component directory.



   1  int
